include ../mixins/head.pug
doctype html
html(lang="en")
	// HTML Head
	+project_head('Astra - Max Nielsen')

	body
		// Header
		include includes/header

		// Title and nav(?)
		picture.project-hero-img.serendipity-hero-img
			source(
				srcset="../../img/design/astra/menu.jpg" 
				media="(min-width: 58.125rem)"
				)
			source(
				srcset="../../img/design/astra/menu.jpg" 
				media="(max-width: 58.125rem)"
				)
			img(src="../../img/design/astra/menu.jpg")
		
		// About Me
		.two-col
			aside(id="table_of_contents")
				h1(id="table_of_contents_title") Astra
				p.tagline
					| Everyday artifacts from a future moon colony monopoly.
				div(id="project_details")
					.project-details.details-border
						.h-btn
							h2.details-title(id="project_details_title") Project details
							a.button-tiny.button-small.button-toggle(
								data-hide-text="Hide" 
								data-show-text="Show" 
								id="project_details_toggle"
								) Hide
						.project-details-wrapper(id="project_details_wrapper")
							.project-for.project-detail-item
								h3 Group project for
								a.button-tiny(
									href="https://sparkjam.design/" 
									target="_blank"
									)
									| Sparkjam 2025
									|   - A design jam
							.project-detail-item
								h3 Timeframe
								p May 2025 (2 weeks)
							.project-detail-item
								h3 Award
								p 3rd place finish and a mechanical keyboard :D
							.project-detail-item
								h3 Project focus
								ul.smaller-list-indent
									li Speculative design &amp; storytelling
									li Physical prototyping
									li AR interface design
							.project-detail-item
								h3 Tools used
								ul.smaller-list-indent
									li Figma
									li Occulus Quest
							.project-detail-item
								h3 The team
								ul.smaller-list-indent
									li
										a.button-tiny(
											target="_blank" 
											href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/irina-ng-035a4b251/"
											) Irina Ng
									li
										a.button-tiny(
											target="_blank" 
											href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sandra-cao-4741922b8/"
											) Sandra Cao 
									li
										a.button-tiny(
											target="_blank" 
											href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mikael-greenwood-5b0654216/"
											)
											| Mikael Greenwood
							.project-detail-item
								h3 What I did
								p
									| I collaborated with the team on the narrative foundation, made our physical artifacts, and used VR as a makeshift solution to test our AR interface.
				#toc.toc
					h2 In this piece
					ul
						li
							a(
								data-target="what_it_is" 
								href="#what_it_is"
								) What it is
						li
							a(
								data-target="dont_rush_to_your_solution" 
								href="#dont_rush_to_your_solution"
								)
								| Don't rush your solution
						li
							a(
								data-target="physical_making" 
								href="#physical_making"
								) Physical making
						li
							a(
								data-target="reflection" 
								href="#reflection"
								)
								| Reflection
						li
							a(
								data-target="check_it_out" 
								href="#check_it_out"
								)
								| Check it out
			#article
				section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="what_it_is")
					h2.heading-underline What it is
					.explanation-wrapper
						div
							p.summary-text
								| For SparkJam (a 
								dfn(aria-label="An event where people rapidly and collaboratively design in a restricted timeframe, creating a final product by the end. Similar to a hackathon, but for design.") design jam
								| ), our team chose to center our project in the speculative design space. 
								| We built a strong narrative foundation imagining a future lunar company “Astra” that has a monopoly on the moon. 
								| From that future, we designed a set of physical objects (a restaurant menu and a credit card) and an augmented reality 
								| interface that lunar citizens use everyday.
						.subheading
							h3.heading-underline Final design
							img(
								alt="Winner-takes-all system" 
								width="2560" 
								height="2464" 
								src="../../img/design/bc/final_interface.webp"
								)
				section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="dont_rush_to_your_solution")
					h2.heading-underline Don't rush to your solution
					.explanation-wrapper
						div
							p Our group chose the “futures track” of SparkJam as we were interested in designing for humans in space. A normal brainstorming session of ideas gave us starting ideas such as what future space mining gear or a space safari tour might look like. However, when we went to present them in a critique session, we realized they held little meaning to us and the world outside of it being linked to one or two current ideas. When we went to build out these worlds further, the design quickly got lost in it. We were stuck tackling this project from the wrong side: trying to design a solution for an empty world/future.
							p This led me to finding the double diamond design process, a popular tool used to support design processes but adapted to speculative design. I pitched this to the team and we started going through the motions with a starting point of designing for lunar life. We talked about our personal ethics, new scientific innovations, lunar business ventures, and more. This kickstarted the double diamond’s first stage of “signal scanning”. From then on, I hosted the next few discussions for the other steps in the process. It took longer than we expected, but building a rich future world based on the present helped us get a lot farther with Astra’s design. I learned the simple and classic lesson that rushing to a solution, even if you’re a little time constrained, is not a good design decision.
								
						.subheading
							h3.heading-underline Double diamond design process. From 
								a(href="https://www.thefountaininstitute.com/blog/the-double-diamond-of-speculative-design" target="_blank") thefountaininstitute.com
								| .
							img(
								alt="Double diamond design process" 
								width="2560" 
								height="2210" 
								src="../../img/design/bc/user_testing_documents.webp"
								)
							h3.heading-underline Final narrative statement.
							img(
								alt="Double diamond design process" 
								width="2560" 
								height="2210" 
								src="../../img/design/bc/user_testing_documents.webp"
								)
				section#physical_making.wrapper-padding.article-section
					h2.heading-underline Physical making
					.explanation-wrapper
						div
							p Our team was desperate to build something physical in SparkJam. We designed a menu and payment card to act as our artifacts from the world, creating physical-digital interactions between the artifacts and the AR interface.
							p We took a trip together to Opus Art Supplies, exploring papers with different thicknesses and transparencies to help convey a sense of futurism and advanced technologies. I spent a few days testing out layering the velour paper we chose to balance the artifact’s flexibility and transparency. As velour couldn’t be printed on, clear printable adhesive sheets were used.
							p One judge mentioned that these items appear like futuristic versions of today’s items. Our goals with these artifacts was to create a balance of digital and physical interaction in our design (something our team values). However, I understand that we should have considered creating more novel artifacts that would have aligned more with communicating Astra’s dystopian narrative and/or had more intentionality behind why they existed.

						.subheading
							h3.heading-underline Iterations of physical artifacts &amp; their interactions with AR
							img(
								alt="Screenshot of digital sticky notes grouped together by a lot of themes" 
								width="2560" 
								height="2210" 
								src="../../img/design/bc/thematic-analysis.webp"
								)
				section#reflection.wrapper-padding.article-section
					h2.heading-underline More design jams please!
					p Sparkjam opened me up to trying a lot of new things: speculative design and world building, physical prototyping, and designing augmented interfaces that interact with physical artifacts. Attending design jams give me the opportunity to try new passions and ideas in a safe space with a group of friends that all want to improve their design skills. It was a bonus that we received 3rd place in the competition. I look forward to attending SparkJam 2026!
				section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="check_it_out")
					h2.heading-underline Check it out
					.explanation-wrapper.figma-embed
						.trailer.subheading
							h3.heading-underline Watch the video
							iframe(
								allowfullscreen="" 
								src="https://embed.figma.com/proto/xbyXBa8LHb7pnpdTC0oVcH/BC-Healthcare-Hub-Slide-Deck?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=1-78&viewport=40%2C600%2C0.09&scaling=scale-down-width&content-scaling=fixed&embed-host=share" 
								height="450" 
								width="800"
								)
						.trailer.subheading.figma-embed
							h3.heading-underline View the process documentation
								iframe(
									allowfullscreen="" 
									src="https://embed.figma.com/proto/xbyXBa8LHb7pnpdTC0oVcH/BC-Healthcare-Hub-Slide-Deck?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=1-78&viewport=40%2C600%2C0.09&scaling=scale-down-width&content-scaling=fixed&embed-host=share" 
									height="450" 
									width="800"
									)
								a.button-small(
									target="_blank" 
									href="../../file/design/bc/BC Healthcare Hub - Slide Deck.pdf"
									) Download static slide deck
						
		// Footer
		include includes/footer